A||||8||pherder||Separating the lenses on a GT the easy way!||||6||
Z||000000||pherder||08-30-2000||07:31 PM||||I found out today the easiest way to remove the lenses from the backing on my 88 GT.<P>Seems if you have 22 days in August of 100 degrees or hotter, the sealant that is "holding" the back to the front is MUCH easier to take apart.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I put on the brand new outer lenses I got from gmpartsdirect and have what looks like brand new rear tail lights.<P>Paul<P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||AL||08-30-2000||09:22 PM||||how much did it cost.||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||08-30-2000||10:21 PM||||16504929 and 16504930 are the GT's outer lense part numbers.<P>IAW <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com," TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com,</A>  the cost is $85.08 plus $11.91 shipping/handling for a total of $96.99 for each side.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||08-31-2000||12:03 AM||||Surprised this one didn't show up as a "hot topic"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000004||mrfiero||08-31-2000||12:22 AM||||This reminds me of an '86 GT I parted out a few years ago.  I stored it outside, next to the garage, and was trying to get the roof panel off (it had a sunroof).  It was July or August and it had been in the high 90's low 100's all week.......I was pulling on one of the A pillars when the windshield fell out!   It was so hot that the sealant melted!  Needless to say the roof panel gave me no fits.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
